    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "4901d962245dd4cf4095f4fc523bedbbe053ab43d7160fb6b656975c0eac5231",
      "text": "Day 2 · After breakfast, congress in the morning.\n\nAfter the congress, discover the vibrant energy and rich history of Buenos Aires on a 4-hour city tour. Begin in the iconic Plaza de Mayo, where the historic Casa Rosada and the Metropolitan Cathedral stand as testaments to Argentina’s past. Stroll through the charming streets of San Telmo, filled with antique shops and tango bars, before the colourful spectacle of La Boca’s Caminito street. Experience the grandeur of Recoleta Cemetery, final resting place of Eva Perón, with its intricate mausoleums, and conclude in the modern neighbourhood of Puerto Madero, where sleek architecture meets waterfront views. With expert guides and comfortable transportation.\n\nIn the evening, dinner and tango show at Michelangelo, with private transfers included.",
